Subject: [PATCH] Keep attribute and range wrappers alive across iteration

GCC 16.2.1 rejects these temporary-wrapper range expressions with
-Werror=dangling-reference. MLIR attributes reference immutable storage owned
by MLIRContext; ContentAttr::getTransformations returns its stored attribute
array. Name the attribute handle or ArrayRef before iterating, making its
lifetime explicit through the loop. Preserve element references, optional
fallbacks, bounds checks and all compiler warnings.

Regression: check-compatibility.py compiles the actual affected translation
units with their generated release flags. Original units fail in the retained
September 7 diagnostic build. No warning option is changed.

--- a/src/vpux_compiler/src/dialect/VPUIP/IR/types/iti_buffer.cpp
+++ b/src/vpux_compiler/src/dialect/VPUIP/IR/types/iti_buffer.cpp
@@ -309,7 +309,8 @@
             return result;
         }
 
-        for (const auto& inHalo : outHalo.getInwardHaloRegions().getValue()) {
+        const auto inwardHaloRegions = outHalo.getInwardHaloRegions();
+        for (const auto& inHalo : inwardHaloRegions.getValue()) {
             const auto inHaloAttr = mlir::cast<vpux::VPUIP::HaloRegionAttr>(inHalo);
             const auto inHaloShape = parseIntArrayAttr<int64_t>(inHaloAttr.getShape());
 
